            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 875)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Source links, fit for production.</b> Set Source Links is its own window now (in front, beside Share This Review, and one click from People). <b>Choose Folder&#8230;</b> points at the delivery on a mounted volume; or paste a direct download, a <b>Google Drive</b> or <b>Dropbox</b> file link (turned into its download form), or <b>one zip of the whole delivery</b>. The window names what each link is and <b>Test</b> asks it &#8212; size, &#8220;a page, not a file&#8221;, &#8220;asks for a sign-in&#8221;, &#8220;not found&#8221; &#8212; before it goes out.</li>
<li><b>One zip serves every clip.</b> A seat without the media fetches the zip once, unpacks it, and finds each clip inside by name &#8212; sequences included. On a slow connection the zip waits as one row in the Network window.</li>
<li><b>Make a Zip for Online Delivery&#8230;</b> zips a chosen folder into your synced Drive or Dropbox folder; paste its share link back.</li>
<li>The invite says where the originals are, and the person sees it when they open it.</li>
<li>Join a Review has a refresh button beside the review menu.</li>
<li>The View menu ticks the zoom it is at.</li>
<li>End Review retries with the review&#8217;s own key when the relay refuses this Mac&#8217;s, and says so plainly if it still can&#8217;t.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
