            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 869)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Name the review.</b> Share This Review has a <b>Review name</b> field &#8212; &#8220;Toyota Highlander&#8221; rather than &#8220;James&#8217;s review&#8221; &#8212; and that is what people see in Join a Review and on invites. The session&#8217;s title is offered to start with.</li>
<li>The Review Manager shows a live review&#8217;s <b>passphrase itself</b>, in its capsule, for reading out &#8212; not only a copy button.</li>
<li>The copy and refresh buttons press visibly now, and the copy button ticks green for a moment.</li>
<li><b>Web review: no colour shift between playing and pausing.</b> The parked still and the live-trim canvas are the reference and take no gamma filter; only the video does, since only the video has the browser&#8217;s lift to correct. Measured on a live review: parked and moving within one level.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
